A||N||6||burdell1||Head Gasket or Piston Gone bad!?||||1||
Z||000000||burdell1||06-01-2000||04:19 PM||||I finally brought my car to get checked out and they said that it was either the head gasket or a piston has gone bad. I know that if it is the piston then I need a new engine. However, what is the cost typically for replacing the head gasket? They told me $700 minimum. Is that sound about right? Time to look for a new car I guess......||||reg||1
Z||000001||87PegasusGT||06-01-2000||06:15 PM||||I took the opportunity to do the 3.4  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||06-01-2000||11:12 PM||||No way.  $700?  Y'can do a head gasket yourself.  Especially if the Fiero isnt your only transportation.  It isnt too hard...dont let any of these guys fool you. Just time.<P>Even the piston isnt a big deal.  If a bonehead like me can rebuild his own engine...<I>anyone can</I>.  Dont let them mechanics scare you.<p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 06-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phaeton||06-01-2000||11:42 PM||||The shop isn't sure if its a head gasket or a piston?  RUN away! to the next nearest shop and have a REAL mechanic look at the Fiero.<P>This isn't an intermittent electrical prob, this is a broke hard part, guess work should not be involved.  Except by us that cannot check the engine first hand.<p>[This message has been edited by Phaeton (edited 06-01-2000).]||||reg||12
Z||000004||DiggityDan||06-01-2000||11:58 PM||||Why don't you start by describing your problems and we can see if some of us here can help you with your problem. <BR>I agree with Phaeton, if a shop can't look at it and tell, they are either idiots or they are trying to jerk you around a little. Either way, do the work yourself or take it to a shop that you know is reputable.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Zman302||06-02-2000||12:17 PM||||If it is only a head gasket, you should be able to do it for alot less than 700.  You should get the head atleast check and the cost of the gaskets, probably set you back about 150.  If the head is cracked, then you might have another 350 in it if you go for a reconditioned head or about 75-150 for a junkyard head.  If it is the 4 cyl, it should take about 4-5 hours taking your time for the entire job.  If it is the 6 cyl, expect alittle more time but it is still a pretty easy job.  Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fret Naught||06-02-2000||12:45 PM||||That is a bunch of hoo haw!!!!,<BR>Find someone with a compression gage and check it out yourself. If the head gasket is blown, between two cylinders, then you will have low compression on both of those cylinders. If it is bad on just one cylinder then the problem is either rings, valves, or a piston. Squirt about a teaspoon of oil in the suspect cylinder. If the compression comes up then you have a ring problem or cylinder score. If the compression doesn't change then you have a bad piston or leaky valves. At any rate when you pull of the head your questions will be answered, you will see a bad piston ,valve or blown gasket right off. 700.00 is too much money for a head gasket replacement. I have seen the guys on this forum talk allot of us through repairs. We will do the same for you.||||reg||8
